In POSIX, it is easy: #include <pthread.h>
int
pthread_create(pthread_t *thread,
       const pthread_attr_t *attr,
             void *(*start_routine)(void*),
             void *arg);

If this routine instead required an integer argument, instead of a void pointer, the declaration would look like this: int pthread_create(..., // first two args are the same
                   void *(*start_routine)(int),
                   int arg);

If instead the routine took a void pointer as an argument, but returned an integer, it would look like this: int pthread_create(..., // first two args are the same
                   int (*start_routine)(void *),
                   void *arg);

